  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "A weather watch means conditions are favorable for severe weather to develop (be prepared), while a warning indicates that severe weather is imminent or already occurring (take action). Watches cover large areas for longer periods, whereas warnings are for smaller, specific areas under immediate threat. Watch (Be Prepared) Meaning: Hazardous weather is possible. The ingredients for a storm are present. Action: Stay alert, check forecasts, and review your safety plan. Purpose: Provides lead time to prepare before hazardous weather strikes. Warning (Take Action) Meaning: Dangerous weather is occurring or imminent. Action: Seek safe shelter immediately, as the threat is real. Purpose: Alerts you to take immediate protective action. Key Differences Summary Watch = \"Maybe\" (Favorable conditions). Warning = \"Right Now\" (Observed or imminent). Think of Tacos: A watch means you have all the ingredients (shells, meat, cheese) to make tacos. A warning means you are eating tacos right now.",
